  "label": "User projected onto the elderly man as the target of age-related mockery",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the elderly man (elderly_man) through the deictic pronoun 'you' in the top text overlay ('you're so old'). This directly addresses the viewer as the subject of the age-related joke, making the user the target of the meme's projection. The user is also implicitly projected onto the concept of 'your first school book' (textual material) as part of the mocking comparison to the Ten Commandments (ten_commandments) inscribed on the gravestone (gravestone_as_symbol).",
